    "created_at": "2017-08-08T23:38:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-08-08T23:38:05Z",
    "body": "> invalidates the request upon receiving a request for the src/srcset change\r\n\r\nDo you mean, invalidates the decode request? Or invalidates some analogue of the \"image's current request\" concept in the spec?\r\n\r\nDo you have any ideas on how to phrase \"request for the src/srcset change\" in the spec? In particular I am concerned about cases like resizing the window and thus causing a different `<source>` in a `<picture>` to apply. My hope was that the spec's current wording, of waiting for the image's current request to change, would take care of all such cases.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
