    "created_at": "2017-08-16T20:41:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-08-16T20:41:52Z",
    "body": "OK, so let's try this...\r\n\r\n- Add a new flag to all images, \"current request invalidated\".\r\n- relevant mutations and environment changes both set \"current request invalidated\"\r\n- Updating the image data resets \"current request invalidated\"\r\n- First step of decode() goes away; it was mostly unhelpful.\r\n- The in parallel step becomes two steps:\r\n  - First, if current request invalidated is true, wait for it to become false\r\n  - Then, do the current step of waiting for one of the various changes, but additionally have a condition that if the current request's URL is the empty string, that also rejects.\r\n\r\nDoes this sound good, all? If it's unclear I can write up the exact spec patch.\r\n\r\nIdeally we'll want tests for the picture case if possible (e.g. using window.open() and window.resize()... probably some exist in web platform tests already for picture in general of this sort).",
