    "created_at": "2017-08-17T23:41:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-08-17T23:41:18Z",
    "body": "> Updating the image data resets \"current request invalidated\"\r\n\r\nYou mean the step that changes the current request resets this flag?\r\n\r\n> Then, do the current step of waiting for one of the various changes\r\n\r\nJust confirming, this is including waiting for it becoming completely available?\r\n\r\n> Ideally we'll want tests for the picture case if possible (e.g. using window.open() and window.resize()... probably some exist in web platform tests already for picture in general of this sort).\r\n\r\nYeah, I'm hoping that if we can improve the spec to the point where we can agree that it's pretty unambiguous and correct. After that, I'm planning on first putting it all of the tests that cover as much of this as I can think of. After that, I'll start implementing changes to make those tests pass. Does that sound reasonable?\r\n\r\n",
