    "created_at": "2017-08-18T15:06:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-08-18T15:06:12Z",
    "body": "> First, if current request invalidated is true, wait for it to become false\r\n\r\nAlso here, what would be the correct implementation of \r\n\r\nimg.src = \"foo\"; // 1\r\nimg.decode().then(...); // 2\r\nimg.src = \"bar\"; // 3\r\n\r\nIf I'm understanding it correctly, then 1 will invalidate the request, the decode will then wait for that invalidation to be cleared, the request will further be invalidated by 3, so then eventually the decode should succeed (and decode \"bar\")?\r\n\r\nThis seems a bit confusing to me, since I would've expected from the javascript code alone for the decode to either succeed with foo or be rejected. But maybe that's fine, as long as it's clear in the spec?",
