    "created_at": "2017-08-18T20:34:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-08-18T20:34:58Z",
    "body": "> You mean the step that changes the current request resets this flag?\r\n\r\nYep.\r\n\r\n> Just confirming, this is including waiting for it becoming completely available?\r\n\r\nIndeed.\r\n\r\n> Does that sound reasonable?\r\n\r\nSounds perfect :)\r\n\r\n> what would be the correct implementation of\r\n\r\nYeah, your interpretation seems correct here. Hmm, that is a bit confusing. But if we want to avoid this, then I think the best solution is to just put the entire algorithm into a microtask---then it will be ordered correctly relative to any src=\"\" settings. That's the first suggestion in the OP.\r\n\r\nMaybe we should just do that? Then the spec fixes would be:\r\n\r\n- Move the entire algorithm into a microtask\r\n- Remove the src/srcset attribute checks as they are broken when picture is involved\r\n\r\nI don't think we'd need the extra request-invalidated flag at all, would we?",
